          explanation: 'Volatility creates a "drag" on compound returns. A -50% loss followed by a +50% gain doesn\'t return you to even, it leaves you at -25%. This volatility drag is why two portfolios with the same arithmetic mean but different standard deviations produce very different ending wealth.'
