            { label: '"The arithmetic mean of 10% overstates compound growth. Due to volatility drag, the geometric mean is closer to 7%. Your $500,000 would more realistically grow to about $1.9 million, still excellent, but I want to set accurate expectations."', consequence: 'Perfect response. You explained the critical difference between arithmetic and geometric mean, quantified the impact of volatility drag, and set realistic expectations. $1.9M is still transformative wealth, honesty doesn\'t mean pessimism.', score: 3 },
            { label: '"Returns are unpredictable so I can\'t give you any estimate"', consequence: 'While uncertainty exists, descriptive statistics exist precisely to give probability-based estimates. Refusing to estimate isn\'t conservative, it\'s unhelpful. Historical data provides a reasonable range of outcomes.', score: 1 }
