            { label: '"Crashes of 20%+ have occurred roughly every 7-10 years historically. With a 15% standard deviation, a 2-SD event (-20%) should be expected periodically. I recommend stress-testing your plan assuming a 30-40% drawdown to ensure you won\'t need to sell during a crash."', consequence: 'Excellent evidence-based advice. You used historical frequency data, connected it to standard deviation, and recommended practical preparation. This is statistics applied with wisdom, acknowledging risk without predicting timing.', score: 3 },
            { label: '"Don\'t worry, the market always goes up in the long run"', consequence: 'While true over 20+ year periods, this dismisses legitimate short-term risk. A client who doesn\'t expect a 30-40% crash may panic-sell during one. The best advisors prepare clients for inevitable volatility using statistical evidence.', score: 1 }
