      { takeaway: 'Standard deviation is the language of risk', detail: 'S&P 500 SD: ~15%. This means typical years range from -5% to +25%. But real returns have fat tails, extreme events occur 5-10x more often than the normal distribution predicts. LTCM learned this lesson at a cost of $4.6 billion.' },
      { takeaway: 'Volatility drag is real and matters', detail: 'The arithmetic mean (10.3%) overstates actual compound growth (geometric mean: ~7%) because losses hurt more than equal gains help. A -50% loss requires +100% to recover. Managing volatility is as important as maximizing returns.' }
