        { term: 'Sharpe Ratio', definition: 'Risk-adjusted return metric: (Return - Risk-Free Rate) / Standard Deviation. Higher is better, more return per unit of risk.', example: 'S&P 500 Sharpe: ~0.4. Medallion Fund: ~2.0+. A Sharpe above 1.0 is considered excellent for any fund.' },
        { term: 'Conditional VaR (CVaR)', definition: 'The average loss in the worst-case scenarios beyond the VaR threshold. Also called Expected Shortfall. Captures tail risk.', example: 'If 95% VaR = -$1M and CVaR = -$5M, the average loss during the worst 5% of days is five times the VaR threshold.' }
