            { label: 'Point out that 2% monthly means ~22% annually, roughly once every 4-5 years. A $100M loss would be 20% of the portfolio. Recommend maintaining current positions and establishing a tail-risk hedging program using options', consequence: 'Outstanding analysis. Converting monthly to annual probability reveals the true frequency. A 20% portfolio loss every 4-5 years is a serious risk that demands hedging. Tail-risk hedging with options costs money in calm markets but prevents catastrophic losses during crises, exactly Taleb\'s successful strategy.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Shut down all trading to eliminate the 2% risk', consequence: 'Zero risk means zero return. The goal of risk management is not to eliminate risk but to understand it, measure it, and ensure the expected return justifies the risk taken. A well-hedged portfolio can accept calculated risks.', score: 0 }
