            { label: 'Use concrete examples and plain language: "Our models show that roughly once every 4-5 years, we could lose $100M+ in a month, similar to what happened to banks in 2008. We\'ve built a hedging program that caps this loss at $50M, at a cost of $3M per year in hedge premiums."', consequence: 'Perfect communication. You translated probability into frequency ("once every 4-5 years"), used a historical anchor (2008), quantified the solution ($50M cap), and stated the cost ($3M/year). Board members can make informed decisions with this information. Clear risk communication prevents the "nobody told us" excuse.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Tell the board "Everything is fine, the models say risk is low"', consequence: 'This is exactly what bank risk officers told boards before 2008. Oversimplification and false reassurance failed catastrophically. Board members deserve honest, clear risk communication to fulfill their fiduciary duty.', score: 0 }
