      'The formula error (dividing by sum instead of average) halved the apparent risk of JPMorgan\'s positions. This gave traders and risk managers false confidence, allowing positions to grow far larger than appropriate. A single cell error in an Excel model contributed to the largest trading loss in banking history: $6.2 billion.'
