        'DCF works by projecting FUTURE cash flow, not just current cash flow. Model when the company will reach profitability (e.g., year 3-4), project FCF growth thereafter, calculate terminal value, and discount everything back. The $50B valuation implies the market expects enormous future cash flow, reverse DCF can tell you exactly how much',
        'Use the price-to-sales ratio instead, since it is the only multiple that works for unprofitable companies and it removes the need to make any assumptions about when cash flow eventually arrives',
