        { term: 'Financial Data Scientist', definition: 'A professional who applies ML, statistics, and programming to financial data to build predictive models, optimize processes, and extract insights from structured and unstructured data.', example: 'A data scientist at Visa building ML models that analyze billions of transactions in real-time to detect fraud, blocking $25 billion in fraudulent charges annually.' },
        { term: 'Fintech', definition: 'Financial technology, the intersection of finance and technology where new products, platforms, and analytical tools are created to improve or disrupt traditional financial services.', example: 'Betterment\'s robo-advisor platform uses ML to provide automated investment management to millions of customers at a fraction of the cost of traditional financial advisors.' }
