            { label: 'Allocate across 3-4 high-quality sources: credit card data ($800K), NLP/sentiment ($500K), web scraping infrastructure ($400K), and satellite for retail positions ($300K), with rigorous backtesting of each source before full commitment', consequence: 'Excellent allocation. Diversifying across complementary data types reduces reliance on any single source. Credit card data covers consumer stocks, NLP covers all stocks, web scraping provides custom signals, and satellite covers physical retail. Backtesting before commitment ensures you only pay for data that actually generates alpha.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Subscribe to 20 cheap data feeds to maximize data volume', consequence: 'Low-cost data feeds typically have low signal-to-noise ratios. Processing 20 noisy sources overwhelms the analytical team and increases the risk of overfitting, finding patterns in noise rather than genuine signals. A few high-quality sources outperform many low-quality ones.', score: 0 }
