            { label: 'Flag the divergence as a risk factor, investigate the specific topics driving the tone shift, reduce position size by 25% as a precaution, and monitor closely for confirming or disconfirming data', consequence: 'Perfect response. The NLP signal is one input, it doesn\'t override everything, but it shouldn\'t be ignored. Investigating the root cause (what topics made the CEO sound cautious?), reducing exposure proportionally, and monitoring for confirmation is exactly how Point72 and Citadel use NLP signals. The signal adjusts your conviction; it doesn\'t replace your analysis.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Immediately liquidate the entire position based on the NLP signal', consequence: 'Overreacting to a single alternative data signal is as dangerous as ignoring it. NLP sentiment is one input among many. It should adjust your risk assessment, not trigger binary decisions. The CEO might sound cautious for personal reasons unrelated to the business. Proportional response is the correct approach.', score: 1 }
