            { label: 'Reallocate the satellite budget to expand the credit card data coverage (more retailers, longer history) and explore one new high-potential data source. Keep satellite data under annual review.', consequence: 'Excellent capital allocation. Doubling down on what works (credit card data with proven alpha) while exploring new frontiers is optimal. Canceling satellite data completely might be premature, an annual review keeps the option open. The discipline to cut non-performing sources and reinvest in proven ones is what separates top alternative data programs from wasteful ones.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Cancel all alternative data subscriptions since one source failed', consequence: 'One data source failing doesn\'t invalidate the entire alternative data approach. Your credit card data is performing well, demonstrating genuine alpha. Canceling everything because one component underperformed is like closing your entire stock portfolio because one stock declined.', score: 0 }
